  "lineage": "Mainland Chinese popular song revived after 1978 as gangtai imports met domestic tongsu singing, hardened into the 1994 Beijing 'new music' generation (Na Ying, Sun Nan, Gao Feng) and then into the post-2005 televised-talent and streaming era dominated by Hunan TV, Modern Sky and Tencent Music — the mainstream form is a 70-100 BPM 4/4 ballad with piano, string pad and programmed kit, declamatory wide-vibrato tongsu vocal projection over Western functional harmony, often with erhu, dizi or guzheng overdubs signalling 'guofeng' national style.",
